## Lore

The Lo-Dox, the Dragon Turtle, looks like a giant winged turtle, and the look deceives. What seems a shell is a thick hide of tough skin and cartilage; there is no lower shell and nothing retracts. A pair of huge black-feathered wings grows from behind the long, thick neck, and the round head carries small bright green eyes, a pug nose and whiskers. Its skin is silvery blue, platinum or bronze.

Lo-Dox are rare on the Palladium World and on most worlds, and known for a cantankerous temper and an intolerance of everyone, dragons included; they seem permanently annoyed, gruff and condescending. Even more reclusive than most dragons, they are drawn into the world of other races by curiosity and a lust for magic and treasure. They love the water, often live at the bottom of an ocean, sea or lake, feel an affinity for aquatic creatures and claim to understand water elementals.

**Alignment:** The vast majority are anarchist or miscreant, but any is possible.

**Size:** 12 feet (3.6 m) tall at the top of the back, 20 feet (6 m) with the head raised, 10-15 feet wide, 20-25 feet long, with a 50 foot (15.2 m) wingspan.

**Weight:** 30 tons.

**Habitat:** Anywhere, preferring oceans, seas and large lakes.

**Average Life Span:** 6000 to 9000 years.

**Enemies:** Many, earned through its vindictiveness. Dislikes other dragons, sea serpents and supernatural beings of any alignment.

**Allies:** None to speak of; Lo-Dox are not very likable.

## GM Notes

The Lo-Dox hatchling is the slow, tough, water-bound dragon with a chip on its shoulder. Its inferiority complex is the hook: tell it it is slower than a real dragon and it will prove otherwise, usually unwisely. Its metamorphosis only reaches aquatic shapes, which limits its disguises on land to a couple of hours.
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'lo-dox-dragon');


-- Read the result back rather than trusting the exit code. d1-apply prints
